    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "These relations form the N = 2 SUSY algebra. It describes SUSY quantum mechanics [38,6]. We can also view it as generators of a Z 2 -grading of a Hilbert space."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 15,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 115.667, 681.667, 328.0, 697.667 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Using these generators it is easy to see that"
  }, {
    "type" : "formula",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Formula",
    "id" : 16,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 273.333, 650.667, 352.0, 666.667 ],
    "content" : "S = q or S = qt"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 17,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 99.667, 618.667, 327.667, 633.0 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "realizes nilpotent S ’s. On the other hand when"
  }, {
    "type" : "formula",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Formula",
    "id" : 18,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 275.0, 587.0, 351.667, 600.333 ],
    "content" : "S = b or $ = f,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 19,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 99.667, 519.667, 525.667, 570.0 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "we obtain projector S ’s. These operators help construct the constant Y ij operator S i S j . They can satisfy either of the three conditions set in (3.9). The corresponding Hamiltonians are either given by (3.4) or (3.8)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 20,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 99.667, 482.333, 526.0, 516.333 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The operator Y ij = S i T j is Baxterized when either one of ST = 0 or TS = 0 is satisfied. This is easily realized using the SUSY generators 4 as"
  }, {
    "type" : "formula",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Formula",
    "id" : 21,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 244.333, 412.333, 525.667, 467.667 ],
    "content" : "S = 9, T =b T = f ST = 0 (3.15)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 22,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 100.0, 321.667, 525.0, 354.0 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The TS = 0 yields the same choices when S and T are interchanged in the above equation. The Hamiltonians in this case are of the form (3.8)."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 23,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 99.333, 270.667, 526.667, 318.333 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "All of the above SUSY realizations are algebraic or independent of the size of the representation of the SUSY algebra. For the C 2 representation the SUSY generators take the form"
  }, {
    "type" : "formula",
    "pdfua_tag" : "Formula",
    "id" : 24,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 220.667, 194.333, 525.667, 257.667 ],
    "content" : "(00) (%) 1 0 ) b = (3.16)"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 25,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 99.333, 119.0, 526.333, 170.333 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "It is clear that these matrices perform a Z 2 -grading of the Hilbert space C 2 , with b and f projecting to the ‘bosonic’ and ‘fermionic’ parts of C 2 . It is also important to note that the C 2 representation of SUSY (3.16) span the space of operators acting on C 2 ,"
